@kapitonov_ivan So $SIVE doesn't handle capacity scaling, Win Semi does volume ramp.

Win is massive. $AVGO, $LITE, $QCOM, Mediatek, $MTSI, $NXPI, all use them. 

They're in $AAPL, SpaceX supply chains too. So volume scaling for hyperscalers is derisked if you secure allocation and do it through Win.

@madridraptor $QCOM was Bytedance and maybe $AMZN if i remember correctly, not $GOOGL TPU. 

I'm really not a fan of how much exposure Qualcomm has to China though. But they made some really important photonics acqusitions like Alphawave (similar to what marvell did with celestial)... for optical networking ip.

So theres upside, just neutral on them. More bullish on mediatek.
